@prefix lgo:  <https://legalgraph.org/ontology#> .
@prefix lgv:  <https://legalgraph.org/vocab/> .
@prefix lg:  <https://legalgraph.org/id/> .
@prefix eli:  <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

lg:NO-EHL a lgo:LegalAct ;
    eli:title "Lov om visse sider av elektronisk handel mv. (ehandelsloven)"@no , "Act relating to certain aspects of electronic commerce (the E-Commerce Act)"@en ;
    lgo:shortName "ehandelsloven" ;
    eli:id_local "Lov 2003-05-23 nr. 35" ;
    lgo:actType lgv:Statute ;
    lgo:jurisdiction lg:NO ;
    eli:date_document "2003-05-23"^^xsd:date ;
    lgo:sourceUrl "https://lovdata.no/dokument/NL/lov/2003-05-23-35"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lgo:reviewStatus lgv:SourceChecked ;
    rdfs:comment "The Norwegian e-Commerce Directive transposition. § 8 is the provider-information duty and § 11 the pre-order disclosure; both follow the directive's Article 5 and Article 10 lists with a narrower professional-detail duty than the ECD minimum."@en .

lg:NO-FREG
    lgo:shortName "foretaksregisterloven" ;
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2017-1132 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://lovdata.no/dokument/NL/lov/2025-06-20-106> ;
    rdfs:comment "In force 1 January 2026, replacing the 1985 register act. § 7-2 is the website identification duty: org.nr and name on nettsider, brev og forretningsdokumenter for every enterprise; AS/ASA add register, organisasjonsform, hovedkontor and under-avvikling status."@en .

lg:NO-MFL
    eli:transposes lg:EU-2013-11 ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://lovdata.no/dokument/NL/lov/2009-01-09-2> ;
    rdfs:comment "§ 10 a is the trader ADR information duty: Norway implemented the ADR directive (EEA annex XIX) in the Marketing Act, not a standalone act. Første ledd covers the website/terms duty; annet ledd is the after-complaint duty on a durable medium."@en .

lg:NO-MEDIE
    lgo:shortName "medieansvarsloven" ;
    eli:id_local "Lov 2020-05-29 nr. 59" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://lovdata.no/dokument/NL/lov/2020-05-29-59> ;
    rdfs:comment "§ 5 is the editorial-media disclosure duty: the editor must ensure the medium states who the editor is and that media users can reach the medium's name, address, email and other direct-contact details. Covers editor-controlled journalistic media, including online outlets."@en .
